    "result_text": "Only one test class exists, and the full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response now includes a `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nI placed each piece of logic where it belongs, matching the codebase's existing separation of concerns:\n\n- **`util/RegionTimezone.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility class owning only the region\u2192IANA table, mirroring how `Postcodes` owns postcode ranges and `CustomerCode` owns the code format. Unknown/null regions resolve to `null`.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getTimezone()`, a derived getter that reuses the existing `getLocality()` (so region resolution stays in one place) and delegates the mapping to `RegionTimezone`. Parallels the neighboring `getLocality()` getter.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` property to the owner schema next to `locality`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name (no mapper change needed).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 `locality` \"NSW\", `timezone` \"Australia/Sydney\") passes, and the full suite is green.",
